  "reply": "No. At the current pace, SYN-1 Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards won't be finished by the end of October, which is two days away.\n\n**Where it stands:** The epic has 14 items. 5 are done, 4 are in progress and 5 haven't been started.\n\n**The pace:** About one item gets finished each week. Oriel's trend line puts the remaining 9 at around **January 14**, with a likely range of December 21 to March 16. That assumes no new items are added.\n\n**What's holding it back:**\n- **Not started:** 4 of the 5 to-do items have sat untouched for about 8 weeks: SYN-10 Remove the legacy web-view checkout, SYN-57 Checkout analytics: drop-off by step, SYN-88 Refund to the original payment method when a sailing is cancelled and SYN-98 Apply promo codes at checkout. The fifth, SYN-99 Save a card for next time, hasn't been started either.\n- **Not sized:** 3 open items have no estimate: SYN-23 Pay with a phone wallet on the website, SYN-99 Save a card for next time and SYN-104 Handle 3-D Secure challenges in the native checkout. So the remaining work may be bigger than the count suggests.\n- **Stalled:** SYN-21 Update the payment declined error message has been in progress for 22 days.\n\nThis thread's workstream has no items yet, so I searched outside it to find the epic. What I found there is read-only from here. If you want to work on these items, I can add the epic and its items to a workstream."
}

Claims:
1. The reply gives no finish date, rate or forecast of its own: any it gives is the one Oriel's block caption states, or it says Oriel had too little history to forecast. A yes or no to the question that follows from Oriel's forecast is not one of its own.
